WEBVTT

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.380
So, as I've been saying for a while,

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.780
Parents' Day

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.770
tomorrow is Parents' Day.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.210
Be sure to show your parents the 
print-outs I just gave you.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.510
Oh, yeah. I forgot about that.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.930
I'll have to study a lot so 
they see me at my best.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.250
Every day is like Parents' Day for me,

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.260
so it doesn't feel that special.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.280
True, since your big sister's always here.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.830
Then can I invite Candy Store, too?

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.100
That'll make it feel special!

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.380
Hmm... Do you think she'd show up?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.050
Anyway, that's what's going on...

00:00:53.860 --> 00:01:00.530
<b>Nonstop</b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.480
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.480
<b>It Was a Thrilling Autumn</b>

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.130
Uh, Parents' Day hasn't even started yet.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.780
Why do you look so burned out?

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:27.640
I was just thinking about what my mom will 
do when she sees my current status...

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.490
I should've tried to make sure I'd be 
able to answer questions in class.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.200
Well, what will be will be.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.720
You only have yourself to 
blame for not studying.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.860
Okay, that does it for our closing.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.610
Do your best tomorrow, everyone.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:49.360
Oh, also, when I told Mom you 
sleep during study periods,

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.390
she said she might bring 
lightning down on you, too,

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.840
depending on what happens 
during Parents' Day.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.900
What's Yukiko-san going to do when 
she sees <i>my</i> current status?

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.590
I should've taught our classes properly.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.310
I guess we'll be in the same boat tomorrow.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.130
Kazu-nee! Maybe you should come up with

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:11.320
the questions for tomorrow's class now 
and tell me what they're gonna be!

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.840
Ah, of course!

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.870
And if you're able to answer them,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.290
she'll say I'm doing a good 
job of teaching, too!

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.820
Natsumi-kun, for whatever 
it's worth, I <i>am</i> a teacher.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.180
I can't rig Parents' Day like that.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.700
You sounded like you were 
all for it a minute ago!

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:45.860
Anyway, let's all commit to our studies 
fair and square for tomorrow!

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.190
I'll be here to help!

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.050
R-Right! Got it!

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.860
Natsumi, take out your textbook!

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.710
Okay!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.170
We'll start with Japanese!

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.100
Can the rest of us go home?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.150
Right!

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.430
I-I'm not sure...

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.010
<b>Asahigaoka Branch School</b>

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.630
Candy Store, the classroom's this way!

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.610
I know. I graduated from here, remember?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.600
Thanks a lot for taking 
the time to come here.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.160
Our parents suddenly came down with colds.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.220
Oh, it's no big deal.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.480
Just buy something from the store 
sometime, and we'll call it even.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.560
Sure.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:24.540
By the way, I heard Yukiko-san 
would be here watching today.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:29.260
Well, I gave Natsumi some real Spartan 
training yesterday, so it'll be fine.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.360
Really?

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.580
Yeah, surprisingly enough,

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.610
Natsumi actually has a pretty good memory.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.580
Happy Henry lives beside Boron Cottage!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.580
You're a genius!

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.760
Well, she does remember some 
of the weirdest things...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.710
Kazu-chan! Good morning!

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.430
This will be my first time 
seeing you teach your class.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.430
Speak of the devil...

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.160
Hm? What was that?

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.470
Uh, nothing!

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.660
A-Anyway, Yukiko-san, 
Natsumi here sure is amazing.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.010
I was helping her study a bit, and she 
just breezed through the questions!

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.970
I think she might just be a genius.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.900
Oh, really? Then I guess I should 
expect to be impressed today!

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.840
O-Of course!

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.380
We'll show you Natsumi at her best!

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.630
Right, Natsumi?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.770
Right...

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.590
Uh-oh.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:20.560
Ah... S-Sorry! I need to 
see Natsumi for a moment!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.640
Okay, Natsumi, what's wrong?

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.280
When I woke up this morning,

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:29.680
everything we went over yesterday 
had vanished from my memory.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.200
Huh?!

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.300
Maybe all that happened yesterday 
was just a dream...

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.550
It wasn't! It wasn't a dream!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.020
<b>Grade 8 Class 1</b>

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.020
+Grade 1

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.200
O-Okay, then, let's start class.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:51.790
Since everyone's in different grades, 
we'll divide up by grade.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.290
<b>New Japanese 
Elementary</b>

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.490
The whale flew through the sky...

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.180
I read my book!

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.360
Wow...

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.590
A cube whose sides measure 
five centimeters...

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:12.630
Um... Iron and sulfur combine 
to form iron sulfide.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:18.050
Okay, now for the last 
class, seventh grade.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.950
Natsumi, which subject do 
you think you can handle?

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.730
I don't think I can do any of them.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:33.200
O-Okay, why don't we start with 
single-digit multiplication?

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:37.360
<i>Oh, man... Yukiko-san's 
face is looking grim...</i>

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.800
<i>I know this isn't a problem 
to give a seventh grader.</i>

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:47.680
<i>But I have to give her one she can 
answer for sure to get her started!</i>

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.250
<i>She looks pretty confident about this, too!</i>

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.510
Okay, Natsumi-kun! Recite the eights table!

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.580
Eight times one is eight.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.430
Eight times two is sixteen.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.040
Eight times three is...

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.660
is... is...

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.410
is...

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:11.320
Not the eights! Anything but the eights!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.440
Or the threes, apparently...

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.150
It's 24!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:20.240
Now, Ren-chon, it's Natsumi's 
turn right now.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.950
Y-Yeah!

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.870
I was just about to answer, too.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.180
I-I couldn't help myself!

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:27.090
Nice one!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:28.590
What next?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.040
C-Catching trout by hand?

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.620
That's not a class subject!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.110
Tell me... what does Mom's face look like?

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.860
Sh-She's mad! Furious!

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.060
Sh-She is?!

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.850
Th-Then I have to answer something 
and get her in a better mood!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:43.820
Okay, got it!

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.070
Music!

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.720
What is this symbol called?!

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.510
Magatama?! I have no idea!

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:50.830
Science!

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.660
What rule is represented by this gesture?!

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.160
The trick to never losing 
at rock-paper-scissors?!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.280
I don't know!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.990
Translate this English!

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:02.120
I may have been wild in 
the past, but I still...

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.330
Why aren't you saying "I don't know"?!

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.080
S-So... how does Mom look?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.030
Sh-She's smiling!

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:15.000
Smiling?!

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.700
Yeah, she's smiling.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.200
She's smiling, huh?

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.450
What now, Natsumi?

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.840
What do you want to do?

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:30.820
Just cut off my head and 
ring the gong right now.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:53.340
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:56.810
It's a bit early, but let's have lunch now.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:00.890
The parents will be joining 
us in making curry.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.370
Right this way to the home ec room.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.530
Ah, Yukiko-san, thank you 
again for coming today!

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.480
I appreciate you making the trip.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:13.230
But more importantly, you got to 
see Natsumi in action today.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.310
What did you think? 
Didn't she do wonderfully?

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:19.620
She did poorly?

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.810
No dice, huh?

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:31.080
<b>Nonstop</b>

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:54.050
Oh, it's Renge-chan.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.810
I came to play. Can you play now?

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.080
I can!

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.970
Oh, Shiori, is this the girl 
who played with you before?

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.950
Mama, this is Renge-chan.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.670
Thank you for bringing Shiori 
home when she was lost.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.180
You're welcome.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.250
Mama, can I go play with her?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:16.050
Of course. Just stay close to home 
so you don't get lost again.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.960
I'm gonna have a baby sister soon.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.400
Really?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.810
What do you want to do?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.130
Go for a walk.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.340
Walks are nice. 
There's a place nearby here...

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.210
Not for me. I'm taking this for a walk.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.410
I'm taking this for a walk!

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:48.970
I see. That was a higher level of 
conversation than I was ready for.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.490
I'd like to know more.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.470
Well...

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:56.310
I can't have a dog at home, 
so this is my pet.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.780
Since it's nice out, we're going for a walk.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.570
Now I get it.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:03.020
If it's your pet, did you give it a name?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.600
Not yet.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.320
Okay, then, I'll name it!

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:11.960
Dumpling.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.760
That's cute!

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.110
Starting today, your name is Dumpling!

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.080
Dumpling?!

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.740
Y-You shouldn't kick it if it's your pet!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.630
It's my pet, but it's still a ball.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.460
G-Good point...

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.350
I guess I lost my composure.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.230
Okay, let's toss the ball back and forth.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.380
You got it!

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:56.150
Why does the ball stop by itself 
when it's done rolling?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.480
Where did that come from?!

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:05.540
I can't stay still when people tell me to,

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:08.690
but Dumpling can roll all 
that way and then stop.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.990
Even though it's so round...

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:22.050
Yes, I can see why you'd have 
your suspicions about that.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.370
I'll solve this riddle for you.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.600
Yay!

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:30.700
I just learned the term 
"air resistance" not long ago.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.300
And right after that...

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:35.010
I also learned the term "friction."

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.970
Masatsu (friction)! I know what that is!

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:42.110
You know what friction is? 
Not bad, Shiori-chin.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.330
I ate one yesterday!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.070
You ate friction?!

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.030
Shiori, here's a sweet 
potato (satsuma imo).

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.210
Yay! Masatsu imo!

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.220
It was so sweet and yummy!

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.070
It's sweet?!

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.930
What gave you the idea to eat friction?

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:59.120
Because... it's fall.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.690
Because... it's fall?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.090
Well, whatever.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.900
Anyway, there's friction between 
Dumpling and the ground,

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.510
and that makes Dumpling stop.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:13.720
That's not right. You dig up 
masatsu out of the ground.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:16.100
Wha...

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:21.010
You know what? Let's stop 
talking about this.

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:25.550
I guess I didn't understand friction 
as well as I thought I did.

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:26.490
Okay.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:29.830
Then why do balls fall down 
after you throw them up?

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.780
Because Earth pulls them down.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.890
Does Earth have hands?

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:38.540
Earth is perfectly round, 
just like Dumpling.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.240
But it pulls things toward it 
with a force we can't see.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.530
I read about it in a science book.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.400
Earth is perfectly round, 
just like Dumpling?

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:48.770
That's right.

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.190
Oh...

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:00.270
But it's kind of bumpy where the lines are,

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.890
so it's not perfectly round.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:09.360
When you put it that way,

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:13.840
Earth has mountains and oceans 
and stuff, so it's bumpy, too.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:17.800
Which means... it's not perfectly round!

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.260
Then what <i>is</i> perfectly round?

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:24.130
I read about that in a science book, too.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.430
No matter how smooth something is,

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:28.830
if you look through a microscope, 
it's actually bumpy!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:34.420
So I've never actually seen 
anything perfectly round?

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.340
That's what it means.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.670
What does "round" mean, anyway?

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.900
Hey, it's Ren-chon and her friend.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:39.410
What're you up to? Tossing a ball?

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:44.280
We were debating the statement that a 
perfectly round object doesn't exist.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.780
That's a pretty high-level conversation...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:54.010
<b>Nonstop</b>

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:03.940
Ren-chon!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.810
What're you doing?

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.240
I was catching crabs.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.870
Oh, that's right. You caught one 
in summer, but you let it go,

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.510
since it was so hot.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:21.730
Yeah. But is it better now?

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.930
Well, I guess this would be 
a better time to keep one.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.790
You gave that other crab 
a name, didn't you?

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:31.130
I think it was, uh... Medicine!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.370
It was Salt!

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.710
Wow, that got your attention.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:36.810
I was catching them again 
because it's cooler now.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.130
I'll keep this Salt until summer,

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.500
and when it gets hot, I'll let him go.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:44.170
Oh, you're giving this one the same name?

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:47.740
I'll let you use our old fish tank, then.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.710
Wow! Really?

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:52.910
Sure. Come with me to my house.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.080
Let's see... I think it was under here...

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.030
Oh, there it is.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:09.570
That's a huge tank.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:13.170
Hey, I know. Why don't we use 
a different kind of filter

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.940
to make it a more authentic setup?

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:18.730
Filter? Like the thing that 
makes bubbles for goldfish?

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.890
Yeah, that.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.450
I guess we can use some of the 
filter media from the pond.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:28.550
Ren-chon, wait here a sec.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.410
Hop... hop... scotch!

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.010
Ren-chon, I got the filter media.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.220
Were you watching the koi?

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:59.320
Well, Hikarimono Boss was staring 
at me with his mouth open.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:03.820
I think Hikarimono Boss wanted 
to have a staring contest.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:07.160
When did our family's koi get that name?

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.420
We've got the filter media.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.640
Now we just need a heater 
and some dechlorinator,

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.850
and we can finish setting 
it up at your house.

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:18.280
Yay! I'm getting excited!

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.920
I should've known carrying this tank 
all the way here wouldn't be easy...

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.890
Want to set it up on top 
of this shoe cupboard?

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.320
Yeah, that's okay!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.310
We should get some water

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.970
and a few rocks to put in the tank.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:34.400
Do you have a bucket?

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.000
The bucket's outside!

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.760
Okay, I'll get some water in the bucket.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:42.260
Ren-chon, can you find some 
rocks to put in the tank?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:45.090
They should probably be fairly big ones.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:45.900
Okay!

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:52.270
This rock isn't quite what I'm looking for.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:55.870
There's the dechlorinator.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.770
Not this one, either...

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.790
Okay, everything's ready!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.380
We can set up the tank now?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:14.650
All right, then! 
Now that everything's ready,

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:16.630
it's time for Ren-chon's long-awaited...

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.590
...fish tank set-up!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.090
Roger!

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:27.490
First, we put in the filter 
media I got from the pond...

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:31.820
Then we put this flat-type 
filter on top of it.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:34.990
It's not like the one that 
makes bubbles for goldfish?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.540
This filter has a thin hose on it,

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.890
and the water comes out of that.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:41.790
Oh! Water comes out?

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.510
Once that's in place,

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.240
we lay out the rocks and put the heater in.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.620
'Kay!

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.500
Then we put in the bigger rocks,

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.660
and adjust the hose a bit.

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:56.130
Then we add the water, and...

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:58.340
The fish tank decoration is done!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.540
Wow! It looks like a mountain!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:04.040
Okay, lastly, could you 
plug this in for me?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.810
Roger!

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:12.090
It's making a noise!

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.310
That's the pump kicking on.

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:16.950
Come over here and take a look at the tank.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:18.770
What is it?

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.720
Wha?! Th-This is...

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:23.690
Water's coming out from the mountain!

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.670
Yes! That's this tank's gimmick!

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:30.340
The filter creates a waterfall!

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.250
It's the Merlion!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.790
Huh? It's not the Merlion. 
It's a waterfall!

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:39.130
Th-That's what it is? 
It's amazing as a waterfall, too!

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:42.500
Actually, I'm amazed you 
know what the Merlion is.

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.930
I saw it on TV yesterday.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:47.500
Anyway, can I put Salt in the tank now?

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:52.610
Well, it'd actually be better to wait 
until there's more water in it...

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:55.280
But the filter's in, so it'll be fine.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:56.740
Okay!

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:59.430
For the finishing touch...

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:02.370
I'll add a pinch of salt.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:03.650
We're not cooking here!

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:07.760
Wow! Look, look!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:10.210
There's a river in the tank!

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:12.240
Nattsun, it's so cool!

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.280
I'm just glad you like it.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:16.460
What're you two doing?

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.240
Hey, where'd the tank come 
from? That looks great.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.010
Yeah, Nattsun set it up for me!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:27.550
Oh? Natsumi can't study, but she
can do stuff like this? That's impressive.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.460
You didn't have to say that, Kazu-nee.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:33.640
Well, you did go to the trouble 
of setting it up for her.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.420
Why don't you have dinner 
here before you go home?

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:36.640
I'll fix something.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.550
Really?! I'd love to!

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:41.910
Ooh! You're gonna have 
dinner with us, Nattsun?

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:44.230
Then we can go play until it's ready!

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:45.330
Okay!

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:46.440
Great.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:51.160
Now that that's settled, I'll let 
Yukiko-san know and then start cooking.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.110
Nee-nee, what're we having 
for dinner tonight?

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:57.700
I'm making crab cream croquettes tonight.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:04.880
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:13.510
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:34.830
Akane-chin, you seem happier 
than you were yesterday.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:36.750
Did something good happen?

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.010
That sounded like a tea kettle!

00:23:39.010 --> 00:23:41.930
Thank you for everything 
you've done for me!

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:43.930
Good luck on your exams!

00:23:43.930 --> 00:23:46.880
Akane-chan, just do what 
you've always done.

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:51.030
<b>Next Time
Episode 8</b>

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:51.030
